{"container":"cdc:Service","handlers":[{"name":"onRead","kind":"remote","signature":"remote function onRead(record {} afterEntry, string tableName) returns error?","required":false,"doc":"Invoked for each row captured during the initial snapshot of a table, before streaming of live changes from the replication slot begins.","params":[{"name":"afterEntry","type":"record {}","required":true,"doc":"The row as captured. Declare a record type to project its columns."},{"name":"tableName","type":"string","required":true,"doc":"Name of the table the row came from, useful when one service handles several tables."}],"returns":"error?"},{"name":"onCreate","kind":"remote","signature":"remote function onCreate(record {} afterEntry, string tableName) returns error?","required":false,"doc":"Invoked when a row is inserted.","params":[{"name":"afterEntry","type":"record {}","required":true,"doc":"The row's state after the insert. Declare a record type to project its columns."},{"name":"tableName","type":"string","required":true,"doc":"Name of the table the change occurred in."}],"returns":"error?"},{"name":"onUpdate","kind":"remote","signature":"remote function onUpdate(record {} beforeEntry, record {} afterEntry, string tableName) returns error?","required":false,"doc":"Invoked when a row is updated, with both the pre- and post-change images of the row. Unless the table's REPLICA IDENTITY is set to FULL, the pre-image carries only the columns that make up the replica identity (the primary key by default), with the rest unset.","params":[{"name":"beforeEntry","type":"record {}","required":true,"doc":"The row's state before the update."},{"name":"afterEntry","type":"record {}","required":true,"doc":"The row's state after the update."},{"name":"tableName","type":"string","required":true,"doc":"Name of the table the change occurred in."}],"returns":"error?"},{"name":"onDelete","kind":"remote","signature":"remote function onDelete(record {} beforeEntry, string tableName) returns error?","required":false,"doc":"Invoked when a row is deleted. Only the pre-change image is available, and unless the table's REPLICA IDENTITY is set to FULL, it carries only the columns that make up the replica identity (the primary key by default).","params":[{"name":"beforeEntry","type":"record {}","required":true,"doc":"The row's state immediately before it was deleted."},{"name":"tableName","type":"string","required":true,"doc":"Name of the table the change occurred in."}],"returns":"error?"},{"name":"onTruncate","kind":"remote","signature":"remote function onTruncate(string tableName) returns error?","required":false,"doc":"Invoked when a table is truncated. No row images are available, only which table was affected.","params":[{"name":"tableName","type":"string","required":true,"doc":"Name of the table that was truncated."}],"returns":"error?"},{"name":"onError","kind":"remote","signature":"remote function onError(cdc:Error cdcError) returns error?","required":false,"doc":"Invoked when the connector fails to capture or dispatch a change event.","params":[{"name":"cdcError","type":"cdc:Error","required":true,"doc":"The failure that interrupted change capture."}],"returns":"error?"}],"rules":[{"requirement":"at least one of","handlers":["onRead","onCreate","onUpdate","onDelete","onTruncate"],"message":"A CDC service must declare at least one change handler. onError alone never receives a change event, so the service would do nothing."}],"note":"attach it to postgresql:CdcListener; declared in ballerinax/cdc — bal discover service Service -p ballerinax/cdc"}
